    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d120">

                <pb facs="0182" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/213</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Carey and Gregory have concluded preliminary contract with Shantung Government
                    for the improvement of the Grand Canal in that province as part of Huai River
                    conservancy. Construction work to be carried out by Carey.</p>
                <p>The Chinese Government, under the Treaty of 1898, felt obliged to offer a
                    participation in loan to Germans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
